\fs32 \cf0 To get 
\f1\b LiDAR scans overlaid with neighborhood parcel boundaries
\f0\b0  for \ul Salt Lake City\ulnone , you need to combine elevation data with property boundary maps. Because these are usually maintained as separate geospatial files, you must download both layers from public state clearinghouses or use an all-in-one commercial mapping platform to view them together.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 1. Free Public Data Sources (DIY Overlay)\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 If you are using GIS software like ArcGIS or QGIS, you can download the highest-quality, official public datasets for free: [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/groups/1508789132952429/posts/1742613179570022/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For LiDAR Data:
\f0\b0  The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.utah.gov/products/sgid/elevation/lidar/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Utah Geospatial Resource Center (UGRC) LiDAR Page}} provides public access to the latest elevation data. This includes the high-resolution 
\f1\b 2023 Salt Lake County dataset
\f0\b0 , featuring Quality Level 1 (QL1) LiDAR at 8 points per meter. You can download the raw point clouds (
\f2\fs28 .laz
\f0\fs32 ) or pre-processed Digital Elevation Models (
\f2\fs28 .tif
\f0\fs32 ). [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.utah.gov/products/sgid/elevation/lidar/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://portal.opentopography.org/lidarDataset?opentopoID=OTLAS.042013.26912.1"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.utah.gov/products/sgid/elevation/lidar/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 For Parcel Data:
\f0\b0  Download the legal property boundaries directly via the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://opendata.gis.utah.gov/maps/utah-salt-lake-county-parcels"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 UGRC Salt Lake County Parcels Portal}} or explore them visually using the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://parcels.utah.gov/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Utah State Parcels Tool}}. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://parcels.utah.gov/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Alternative Point Cloud Downloads:
\f0\b0  You can also use the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://portal.opentopography.org/datasetMetadata?otCollectionID=OT.122014.26912.1"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 OpenTopography Wasatch Front Portal}} or the USGS LiDAR Explorer to highlight an area of interest on a map and download the raw underlying elevation point data. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://portal.opentopography.org/datasetMetadata?otCollectionID=OT.122014.26912.1"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apps.nationalmap.gov/lidar-explorer/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bOiI3CRp_XE&t=1"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://maps.cteco.uconn.edu/data/flight2023/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 4}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 2. Immediate Online Streaming (No GIS Software Required) [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://extension.unh.edu/resource/start-making-maps-lidar-online-workshop"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 If you want to view or stream the LiDAR point cloud directly over neighborhood parcels in your web browser without downloading massive datasets:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Equator Studios:
\f0\b0  The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.equatorstudios.com/utah_saltlake/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Equator Salt Lake County Portal}} has pre-loaded both the Salt Lake County parcel boundaries and historical LiDAR datasets into a streamlined browser environment. This allows you to inspect zoning, year built, and 3D terrain variations simultaneously, or export them into CAD/DWG formats. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.equatorstudios.com/utah_saltlake/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://equatorstudios.com/equator-launches-salt-lake-city-lidar-data/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.equatorstudios.com/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 4}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

