\f1\b\fs32 \cf0 \cb8 Yes, \ul Oregon\ulnone  and \ul California\ulnone  both offer similar, high-quality public LiDAR and neighborhood parcel resources.
\f0\b0 \cb1  However, while Oregon shares Utah\'92s highly centralized, public-access model, California's data is slightly more fragmented due to its size and privacy restrictions. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=f937000d00c340fb8b502fdd16e30882"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
Both states provide excellent alternatives to Utah's UGRC, broken down by how you can access them:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 1. Oregon Geographic Resources\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 Oregon is a leader in public LiDAR data. Its resources are highly centralized and completely free to the public, much like Utah's system. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oregon.gov/dogami/lidar/pages/index.aspx"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 LiDAR Data:
\f0\b0  The 
\f1\b Oregon Department of Geology and Mineral Industries (DOGAMI)
\f0\b0  manages the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oregon.gov/dogami/lidar/pages/index.aspx"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Oregon Lidar Consortium}}. You can use the interactive {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.dogami.oregon.gov/maps/lidarviewer/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 DOGAMI Lidar Viewer}} to visually inspect high-resolution topography, hillshades, and bare-earth imagery across the state. You can also download 7.5-minute quadrangle data for free. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.dogami.oregon.gov/maps/lidarviewer/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.oregon.gov/dogami/lidar/pages/index.aspx"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://researchguides.uoregon.edu/oregon-lidar-elevation/accessing-oregon-lidar"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=81d77045337e44f59f545f71554e934a"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 4}}]\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Parcel Data:
\f0\b0  Oregon manages the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ormap.net/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 ORMAP Project}}, which provides a centralized, digital base map of property tax lots across all counties. You can view local neighborhoods on the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ormap.net/gis/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 ORMAP GIS Map Viewer}} or pull normalized datasets directly from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://geohub.oregon.gov/pages/parcel-viewer"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Oregon GEOHub Parcel Portal}}. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ormap.net/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ormap.net/views/aboutUs.html?timestamp=1573259405775"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://geohub.oregon.gov/pages/parcel-viewer"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 2. California Geographic Resources\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 California has extensive geospatial data, but because property records are managed locally by 58 separate county assessors, it requires navigating different portals depending on your exact focus.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 LiDAR Data:
\f0\b0  In December 2025, the California Natural Resources Agency launched a massive statewide program called the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wildfiretaskforce.org/california-unveils-first-ever-statewide-lidar-maps/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Wildfire, Ecosystem Resilience, and Risk Assessment Initiative (WERK)}}. This program made over 100 million acres of high-resolution vegetation and canopy 3D LiDAR available via the Wildfire Science & Technology Commons. For purely topographic bare-earth terrain data, you can search the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.data.ca.gov/search?layout=grid&tags=lidar"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 California State Geoportal LiDAR Catalog}}. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://wildfiretaskforce.org/california-unveils-first-ever-statewide-lidar-maps/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.data.ca.gov/search?layout=grid&tags=lidar"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}]\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Parcel Data:
\f0\b0  California lacks a perfectly open, unlimited public parcel repository due to privacy law restrictions (like the Privacy Act of 1974). However, CAL FIRE hosts the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=f937000d00c340fb8b502fdd16e30882"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 California Statewide Parcels Public Layer}}, which provides public, standardized property outlines, site addresses, and Assessor Parcel Numbers (APNs) across the state. For deeper property data (like owner names or sales history), you usually have to visit the specific county assessor's GIS website (e.g., LA County Open Data, San Francisco Property Map). [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=f937000d00c340fb8b502fdd16e30882"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs40 \cf0 3. All-in-One Multi-State Alternatives\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs32 \cf0 If you prefer not to jump between different state web portals, you can use the same universal platforms mentioned for Utah:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The USGS National Map:
\f0\b0  The federal USGS LiDAR Explorer provides 3DEP elevation data for both Oregon and California.\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Commercial Streaming:
\f0\b0  Automated web tools like the Equator Studios Portal stream pre-aligned parcel maps and LiDAR layers for specific counties in both states (for example, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.equatorstudios.com/california_sanmateo/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 Equator San Mateo County Portal}}) without needing any GIS installations. [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://gis.equatorstudios.com/california_sanmateo/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usgs.gov/faqs/what-lidar-data-and-where-can-i-download-it"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.facebook.com/groups/487042914784182/posts/3268178723337240/"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
