\fs32 \cf0 The resolution, detail, and data density of these public LiDAR resources are generally measured by two standard industry metrics: 
\f1\b Aggregate Nominal Pulse Density (ANPD)
\f0\b0  (how many laser points hit each square meter) and 
\f1\b Digital Elevation Model (DEM) Resolution
\f0\b0  (the pixel size of the processed bare-earth raster). [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usgs.gov/ngp-standards-and-specifications/lidar-base-specification-collection-requirements"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storymaps.arcgis.com/stories/6f2f3ae997ec4fd3a6f0b31d1ce8bdcb"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usgs.gov/3d-elevation-program-standards-and-specifications"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
Most state agencies conform to the federal {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usgs.gov/3d-elevation-program"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP)}} standard, classifying data by Quality Levels ranging from 
\f1\b QL2
\f0\b0  (standard) to 
\f1\b QL1
\f0\b0  (high-density). [{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usgs.gov/ngp-standards-and-specifications/lidar-base-specification-collection-requirements"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 1}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.usgs.gov/3d-national-topography-model/expired-fy26-3dep-data-collaboration-announcement-dca"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 2}}, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://pubs.usgs.gov/publication/cir1553/full"}}{\fldrslt \cf3 \ul \ulc3 \strokec3 3}}]\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

