\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Utah's 
\f1\b QL1 urban data
\f0\b0  is perfectly suited for digital twins because the point density (8+ pts/\\(\\text\{m\}^\{2\}\\)) is tight enough to cleanly trace roof shapes (e.g., gables vs. flat roofs) and distinct property walls.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
