\f1\b\fs32 \cf0 Step B: Optimize for Web Streaming\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf0 Raw cropped 
\f2\fs28 .LAZ
\f0\fs32  files are still too heavy to stream seamlessly to a browser. You need to convert the output into an octree structure using 
\f1\b PotreeConverter
\f0\b0  (another open-source CLI tool). This breaks the 3D data into tiny tiles, loading only what the homeowner looks at (Level of Detail streaming).\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf0 ruby\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs28 \cf0 # Inside your Sidekiq job after the PDAL crop finishes:\
system("PotreeConverter /data/output/twin_#\{homeowner_id\}.laz -o /data/public/twins/twin_#\{homeowner_id\}")\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

